    "notes": "Rattail: big head with large eyes, a conical snout overhanging a small underslung mouth, a short deep trunk and a long tapering 'rat tail' with no real caudal fin; high first dorsal, long low second dorsal and anal fins; brown with a bluish belly. Approximations: the caudal fin is a 1-unit stub at the tail tip; the chin barbel and the fin rows along the tail are not modelled (the anal fin sits at the rear of the trunk)."
